INT. BOTANICAL CONSERVATORY, AFTER CLOSING - NIGHT

A cathedral of glass and iron. Palms rise into the dark like columns. Condensation drips from the vaulted panes. A path of wet slate winds between orchid beds, and a single lamp near the fountain draws a small circle of gold in the green gloom.

Five people stand in the circle, looking at the water.

PROFESSOR HENRIETTA VAN DER MEULEN-ASANTE (60s) holds a clipboard against her chest like a shield. Beside her, DR. IGNATIUS BELLAMY-OJO (50s) polishes his spectacles on his tie. DOROTHEA "DOT" KWESI-PEMBERTON (30s, gardener's overalls) stands with her arms folded. Across the fountain, SUMNER HALE-ABIOLA (40s, security uniform, flashlight) shifts his weight. And at the edge of the light, the youngest, CELESTINE OYELOWO-STRAND (20s, a notebook against her hip), is writing.

HENRIETTA
Someone moved the orchid.

DOT
It's not an orchid, Professor. It's a hybrid.

HENRIETTA
Dorothea, I do not need a lecture.

IGNATIUS
Henrietta, please. We're all tired.

SUMNER
I locked the east door at nine.

CELESTINE
(not looking up)
And the west?

SUMNER
West too.

HENRIETTA
Then how did it leave the building?

DOT
It didn't.

Silence. A drop falls from the glass into the fountain. Ripples spread.

IGNATIUS
Dorothea, what do you mean?

DOT
I mean it's still here.

She points. At the base of the tallest palm, in the shadow beyond the lamp, something small and pale lies in the soil. The roots of the palm have curled around it like a fist.

SUMNER
(whispering)
That's impossible.

CELESTINE
(finally looking up)
It's not impossible. It's what it does.

HENRIETTA
Celestine?

CELESTINE
It's a hunter. It leaves, then it comes back for what it wants.

Dot unfolds her arms. Ignatius puts on his spectacles. Sumner raises the flashlight, and its beam swings across the glass, across the palms, and settles on the pale thing at the roots.

It is a human hand.
